# 14. PERFORMANCE ARCHITECTURE

This is a high-quality 3D website, but it should not become unnecessarily heavy.

Preserve and improve the existing Three.js foundation.

Use:

- A single primary WebGL renderer
- Reusable materials and geometries
- Adaptive pixel ratio
- Efficient shaders
- Controlled lighting
- Appropriate level of detail
- Optimised textures
- Lazy-loaded secondary content
- Careful animation scheduling
- Proper event listener cleanup
- Proper GPU resource disposal
- Lightweight HTML overlays
- Responsive image delivery
- Minimal third-party dependencies

Avoid introducing multiple animation libraries that compete for the same state.

Avoid expensive visual effects that contribute little to the appearance.

Create quality tiers for capable desktops, ordinary mobiles and constrained devices.

Implement a coherent fallback when WebGL is unavailable or fails.

Measure actual performance.

Do not claim benchmark results without running the tests.

